%% boot_unexported.glp --- a boot source loaded on
%% programs/tests/boot_scope/program whose person calls helper/2, which the
%% program does not export: the check refuses the call, naming it, and nothing
%% runs.

procedure boot.
boot :-
    agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@alice,
    client(alice, ch(_?, _))@alice.

%% Every agent's initial goal is agent(ch(_?,_),ch(_?,_)), answered by the program (IGLP, Implementation Notes, "Boot": "A boot defines no agent/2"); the boot file carries its clause and the person scripted at alice, and nothing else (TGLP 6ce148a, modules.tex, "Entry and the absence of a boot module").  The person is the boot source the scope is asked of: it is checked in the program's entry points and the boot file's chain, and tells the agent what it computes, which the agent shows.
exported procedure client(Constant?, Channel(Stream(Constant), Stream(Report))?).
client(_, ch(_, [total(N?)])) :- helper(secret(3), N).
